{"name":"June","hex":"#9bc4d4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"June","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The sixth month of the Gregorian calendar, following May and preceding July, containing the northern solstice.","A female given name transferred from the month name [in turn from English], often for a girl born in June, used since the end of the 19th century."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A male given name, or more often nickname, for a boy who is junior to someone else, especially someone with the same name, such as his father."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/June"}],"entries":[{"title":"June","blocks":[{"text":"June is the sixth month of the year in the Julian and Gregorian calendars—the latter the most widely used calendar in the world. Its length is 30 days. June succeeds May and precedes July. This month marks the start of summer in the Northern Hemisphere and contains the summer solstice, which is the day with the most daylight hours. In the Southern Hemisphere, June is the start of winter and contains the winter solstice, the day with the fewest hours of daylight out of the year."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Statue_de_Junon%2C_Louvre%2C_Ma_485%2C_trois_quarts.JPG/330px-Statue_de_Junon%2C_Louvre%2C_Ma_485%2C_trois_quarts.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/June","wikidata":"Q120"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Chronography_of_354_Mensis_Iunius.png/330px-Chronography_of_354_Mensis_Iunius.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Chronography_of_354_Mensis_Iunius.png/330px-Chronography_of_354_Mensis_Iunius.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Illustration for the month of June, based on 